# Weight profile flint-exl3-6.0: Recursive's Flint in our EXL3 pack at 6.0 bpw: every projection at 6 bits, head 8
# (exllamav3 1.6.2 + our Flint architecture, mul1 codebook; the routed experts' up projections stored divided by 128,
# quantization_config.expert_interm_div; 30.5 GB), from RecursiveSI/flint at revision 2a247be0. Against BF16
# (8 held-out rows x 1,024): KL 0.051, top-1 91.6 %, ppl 30.07 against 29.88, where two BF16 forwards of the same
# weights already differ by KL 0.034. Measured on the Spark (2026-10-22, SPD-145/144, 512 greedy tokens, one request):
# plain decode 97.4-97.7 tok/s, with the lookup up to 353.4 tok/s on a copy ask; prefill 5,045 tok/s at 4,096 tokens;
# 28.5 GiB at load. The pack is public, pinned by commit. Switch with ops/use-profile.sh flint-exl3-6.0.
QSE_FLINT_VARIANT=exl3-6.0
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Flint-EXL3-6.0
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=17e16040a25bd253ec96f7954feb57cbb996d6b7
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=30.5
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=66
# the engine's limits. Ceiling: the weights (28.5) + the runtime (2.5) + the KV at 262,144 tokens (7.2) + the caches;
# peak: the ceiling + a 4,096-token prefill chunk's workspace at 256k (8.4 GiB over the weights and KV measured on 4.0)
MEM_CEILING_GIB=50
MEM_PEAK_GIB=56
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_flint.env"
